The bug was caused by the logic in the `FreqProxTermsWriter` that allowed the deletion of a term from one field to incorrectly affect documents in another field. When attempting to delete a term, the implementation did not properly account for the context of the field, leading to unintended deletions when terms shared names across different fields.

