```java
if (terms != null) {
  termsEnum = terms.iterator(termsEnum);
} else {
  termsEnum = null;
}
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that if there are no terms for the current field (`terms` is null), the `termsEnum` is explicitly set to null. This prevents any operations on `termsEnum` for a non-existent field, thus avoiding accidental deletions across different fields when terms share the same name. This enforces that deletions occur only within the correct field context.

